00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.520
objection stems from a misunderstanding

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.049
of how weather differs from climate

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:05.240
weather refers to local changes over

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.250
short periods of time such as minutes

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.959
hours days or weeks

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:11.030
typical examples of whether include rain

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.970
clouds snow wind and thunderstorms

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.430
climate refers to longer-term averages

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.140
and maybe regional or global in scale

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.790
and can be thought of as weather

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.460
averaged over an extended period of time

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.260
typically years or decades an easy way

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.150
to remember the distinction is weather

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.200
is what you get

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.520
climate is what you expect

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.220
now that we have a good

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.640
understanding of how climate

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:31.760
and weather differ

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.870
let's look at the scientific consensus

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.600
over ninety seven percent of actively

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.220
publishing climate scientists agree that

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.350
climate warming trends over the past 100

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.090
years are extremely likely to have been

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.420
caused largely by human activity that

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.020
number goes up to over ninety-nine percent

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:46.310
if you include climate

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.540
scientists who have not recently

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.640
published scholarly articles most of the

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.170
